OL,3,GNEWSAWoman's first go at CPR saves
OL,4,Apartner's life
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman's quick thinking helped save
OL,7,Fthe life of her partner after he
OL,8,Fsuffered a cardiac arrest in his sleep.
OL,10,FSophie Bettles, from Underwood,
OL,11,FNottinghamshire, woke to discover Jack
OL,12,FDennis, had gone into cardiac arrest
OL,13,Fand immediately began performing CPR.
OL,14,FDespite having no previous experience,
OL,15,Fshe managed to restart his heart before
OL,16,Femergency services arrived.
OL,18,FJack, 25, suffered a second cardiac
OL,19,Farrest while paramedics were treating
OL,20,Fhim, requiring nine shocks from a
OL,21,Fdefibrillator before his heart began
OL,22,Fbeating effectively again.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
